# `__AOH_MODULE_NAME__` module

__AOH_MODULE_DESCRIPTION__

An ops-hub feature module: Go backend service, typed REST client,
TypeScript types, and Svelte SDK colocated for atomic cross-package
changes.

## Packages

| Package | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-service` | `service/` | Go service (the backend) — see `service/README.md` |
| `@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-types` | `types/` | TypeScript mirrors of the wire DTOs |
| `@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-client` | `client/` | Typed `fetch`-based REST client |
| `@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-web-sdk` | `web/` | Svelte UI components / providers |

Plus operational artifacts:

| Artifact | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Compose snippet | `deploy/compose.snippet.yml` | Hub-stack include for the Go service + its DB |

## Architecture

Consumer apps depend on the SDK; the SDK depends on the client; the
client depends on the types; the service runs independently:

```
consumer apps
    │
    ▼
@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-web-sdk        (Svelte components, providers)
    │
    ▼
@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-client     (typed fetch wrapper)
    │
    ▼  HTTP/JSON
__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-service               (Go, chi + sqlx)
    │
    ▼  SQL
Postgres
```

The TS-side dependency chain is one-way: `web → client → types`.
`types` is consumed by the client and re-exported through the SDK.
`service` has no dependency on the TS packages — it's the runtime, the
TS side is the consumption surface.

## Where to start as a contributor

* Backend feature: `service/AGENTS.md` (agent rules + conventions)
* Wire types: edit `service/internal/dto/*.go` + `types/src/index.ts` in lockstep
* Operational change: `deploy/compose.snippet.yml`
* UI components: `web/`
